# ---- hub-lease epoch re-validation (BH-1023, ships dark) ----
# With this OFF (the default), `bin/hub-lease.sh check` answers from
# state/hub-lease.json whenever that file is younger than HUB_LEASE_CACHE_S, so
# a promote is invisible to the box that just lost the lease until its next
# renew 409s — up to a minute of two boxes both believing they are the hub.
# With it ON, a fresh cache that says held=1 is re-validated against the row and
# `check` additionally requires the row's epoch to still equal the cached one.
# The unreachable-worker paths are identical in both modes (600s grace for the
# current holder, then one ALERT), and a cache that says held=0 never makes a
# request either way.
# The FLEET switch is the pause_flags row, reconciled into
# flags/hub-lease-epoch-check by the once-a-minute renew lane:
#   bin/jobs-client.sh flag-set hub-lease-epoch-check on  "BH-1023"
#   bin/jobs-client.sh flag-set hub-lease-epoch-check off "BH-1023"
# This variable is the BOX-LOCAL override and wins over the file both ways:
# 1 forces the re-validation on, 0 is the kill switch. Unset = the file decides,
# and so does any other value. bin/hub-lease.sh reads this ONE variable out of
# this file itself, because the gated hub lanes are bare crontab lines that source
# nothing — so setting it here takes effect on the next minute's lanes, with
# nothing to restart. Leave the line commented to stay on the fleet switch: a
# commented line is not a setting.
# The read takes the line however you write it: `export HUB_LEASE_EPOCH_CHECK=0`,
# an indented line, a trailing `# comment`, a trailing tab and a CRLF ending all
# resolve the same. If the file carries the variable twice the LAST line wins,
# the way sourcing the file would — so appending the kill switch under a line
# that is already here is a valid way to set it.
# A value it cannot resolve to 1|0 is not an override either, but it writes a
# `knob: HUB_LEASE_EPOCH_CHECK=<v> ignored` line into logs/hub-lease.log — once
# per incident, behind flags/alerted-hub-lease-knob, cleared as soon as the knob
# resolves — so a typo here is visible instead of silent.
#HUB_LEASE_EPOCH_CHECK=1

